  "articleBody": "Upgrading your garage interior transforms daily convenience, but there is a clear boundary between simple shelving and projects that require professional general contracting.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n- Breaker Panel Tripping: If using a shop compressor, power tool, or space heater routinely trips circuits, you need dedicated electrical runs rather than extension cords.\n- Cold, Drafty Stud Bays: Adding heating to an uninsulated space wastes energy; proper thermal insulation and vapor barriers must be installed to code.\n- Wall Moisture and Water Stains: Staining along the slab edges or lower drywall indicates drainage or envelope issues that must be corrected before installing cabinetry.\n- Heavy Overhead Storage Needs: Bolting high-capacity storage racks into ceiling joists requires evaluating roof truss loads so you do not compromise structural ties.\n- Gas Heater Installations: Adding a vented or radiant heating unit demands safe clearance distances, venting, and trade permits.\n\nWorking with an experienced contractor keeps your garage safe, durable, and comfortable in all seasons. Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC leads hands-on drywall, carpentry, and coordinated trade upgrades across the Denver area. Call 303-505-0866 to get an estimate for your garage interior upgrades.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}